033-edit","invocation":{"verb":"edit","touched":[".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"],"args":{"before":"| Which C function does each luajs PACK primitive re-implement — and which LuaJIT library functions does the pack lack? | `nvim --headless -u NONE -l tools/packmap.lua <luajit git dir> [--rev <commit>] [--pack <pack.js>] [--json <out>]` — `cartograph.luajs.packmap`, every pairing DERIVED: the ORACLE's revision (its `jit.version` patch = its commit time), LuaJIT's registrations read as its own buildvm_lib.c reads them (config gates from the oracle), joined against the oracle's live library (the two readings must agree); C bodies by cartograph's C extraction of the PREPROCESSED tree (LuaJIT's own make generates its buildvm headers and names its compile flags); the pack enumerated under node through its own `pairs`. Joins per unit: `lib` name, `mm` metamethod, `msg` (a LuaJIT ERRDEF ASSEMBLED from the unit's string literals, composed with LuaJIT's own slot-free texts), `cite`; the VM's `extern` calls rank the interpreter's handlers first; per primitive, the messages its handler can raise that the pack never says; helpers aligned by co-occurrence (strict only); message drift. MEASURED 2026-09-30 at fbb36bb6: 162 registered = 162 in the oracle; the pack has 85 PRESENT = 74 implemented (59 hand-written, 10 host, 5 transliterated) + 11 refused stubs, 62 method-table functions a frontier; found CART-1217 (no __index loop limit), CART-1218 (the 77 missing), CART-1219 (a Lua 5.2 message). CART-1211 |","file":".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md","after":"| Which C function does each luajs PACK primitive re-implement — and which LuaJIT library functions does the pack lack? | `nvim --headless -u NONE -l tools/packmap.lua <luajit git dir> [--rev <commit>] [--pack <pack.js>] [--json <out>]` — `cartograph.luajs.packmap`, every pairing DERIVED: the ORACLE's revision (its `jit.version` patch = its commit time), LuaJIT's registrations read as its own b